 still unknown"], "rationale": "Rhode Island's eight-point Democratic lean and long record of backing Democratic presidential nominees anchor the call, and the term-limited Republican incumbent removes any incumbency offset. With no polls or ratings published, the expected margin stays close to the state's underlying partisanship.", "watch": "Fresh general-election polling, the identity of the major-party nominees, or a shift in the national mood could move Rhode Island's margin in either direction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Rhode Island is a reliably Democratic state in presidential politics, and its partisan lean of roughly eight points Democratic sets the starting point for this open-seat contest. With the sitting Republican president term-limited, neither party carries an incumbency advantage into the general election.\n\nNo general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are yet available, so expectations rest on the state's underlying partisanship alone. That points to a meaningful Democratic edge with wide uncertainty, since the national environment and the eventual nominees could move the result. Rhode Island's shift of its 2028 primary to March shapes the nominating contest but not the general-election picture.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8249, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7734, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7988, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7688, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8114, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8082, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7696, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0